  "reason": "Unselected seed-domain compatibility proposal. Current approved b65d3ab8/version4.1.0 accepts signed integer seeds through GenCtx/stable_rng, and public runtime.generate requires a literal integer seed without restricting its sign. Proposed14022562 preserves version4.1.0 but rejects all negative seeds; this changes lawful behavior despite the unchanged-legal-generation claim. Rebase validation/tests/notes to preserve signed integer seeds, or explicitly justify a deliberate contract migration. Reported100 paired draws establish parity only for that sampled cohort,not the whole pre-existing seed domain. Retain proposed12/12 resumed battery,70 portable/fresh tests,300 lessons/1200 unique inputs/1200 rotations with zero declared-rival ambiguity solely with proposed bytes. border_policy recolor/preserve prototype has four complete Racket-backed episodes/seeds0..3; all demos/query distinguish settings,default program exactly canonical. Bounded border-witness profile evidence only. Current malformed-scalar weakness is not claimed fixed; no selected source/rule modification,prototype count increment,approval upgrade,submitted-code execution or training admission.",
